data/*.db
data/*.db-*
node_modules/
data/releases/*/*.tmp

# Firmware images stay out of git by default — they arrive every time a version
# is cut and history does not need them.
data/releases/*/*.bin

# EXCEPT the current web-flash images, un-ignored by exact version below.
#
# The exception has to be a real negation, not `git add -f`. Git stops applying
# .gitignore to a file once it is tracked, but Railway's uploader matches the
# patterns literally and knows nothing about tracking — so a force-added image
# is committed and still silently missing from the deploy, which is exactly how
# an hour went. Pinning the version rather than globbing webflash-*.bin also
# keeps superseded builds from being swept into the upload.
#
# They are what the public
# /flash page installs, and the page checks for them before it opens at all.
# `railway up` honours .gitignore as well as .railwayignore, so an image that is
# merely ignored never reaches the deploy and the flasher reports itself closed.
#
# GitHub Releases cannot stand in for this: release assets carry no
# access-control-allow-origin and redirect to a URL that expires within the
# hour, so a browser cannot fetch one cross-origin. They are published there
# too, for anyone who would rather use esptool.
#
# Cutting a release: build with PUBLIC_SERVER_URL, then update the two lines
# below to the new version, `git rm --cached` the old images, `git add` the new
# ones, and redeploy. Verify with a real request afterwards — a 200 on the
# manifest does not mean the image beside it arrived.
!data/releases/amoled18/webflash-0.3.0.bin
!data/releases/epaper154/webflash-0.3.0.bin

# The current AMOLED OTA has passed a real network update on Doreen. Keep the
# exact image available to `railway up`; superseded OTA images stay ignored.
!data/releases/amoled18/0.3.1.bin
